<h1>Tug analysis: duty-cycle energy and hybrid sizing</h1>
<p>Draft for maintainer review</p></header>

<section id="summary"><h2>1 Executive Summary</h2>
<p>The tug analysis module is a set of preliminary performance calculations. Analysis is performed to determine the ideal energy and battery discharge required by a public duty-cycle example; key results are summarized below.</p>
<ul><li>The duty cycle can be used as a calculation example.
<ul><li>The cycle requires $total_energy_kwh kWh, with peak demand of $peak_power_kw kW.</li>
<li>At the assumed engine baseline of $baseline_engine_kw kW, peak battery discharge is $battery_power_kw kW and discharge energy is $battery_energy_kwh kWh.</li></ul></li>
<li>A battery specification cannot be selected from these results alone.
<ul><li>Recharge, conversion losses, reserve and ageing are not evaluated; installed battery capacity remains NOT_EVALUATED.</li>
<li>No tug operating approval is established.</li></ul></li></ul>
<p>The numerical basis is the <a href="#source-example">public example</a>; the interpretation is conditional on the <a href="#assumptions">data register</a>.</p>
