<h3 id="locators">9.2 Source register and calculation access</h3>
<ul><li id="source-theory">OpenStax, University Physics Volume 1, 2016 edition, section 7.4, Power: equations 7.10 and 7.11 define average and instantaneous power; the following unnumbered relations give constant-power work and <a href="https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-4-power">the time integral of power</a>. Consulted for the energy definition; no empirical battery coefficient is taken from this source.</li>
<li id="source-example">Public regression fixture: <code>tests/tug/duty_cycle.json</code>. Both the report generator and <code>TestEmissions</code> in <code>tests/tug/test_tug_toolkit.py</code> read these illustrative inputs.</li>
<li id="source-api">Implementation: <code>src/digitalmodel/tug/emissions.py</code>, documented <code>OperatingPhase</code>, <code>cycle_energy</code>, <code>size_hybrid</code> and <code>HybridSizingResult</code>. Inputs are installed power in kW, phase fractions and durations in h, and baseline fraction. Outputs are energy in kWh, power in kW and a dimensionless energy share.</li>
<li id="source-tests">Existing evidence: <code>tests/tug/test_tug_toolkit.py</code>. Report checks: <code>tests/tug/test_module_report.py</code>. The original energy fixture is illustrative; its presence does not establish field validation.</li>
<li>Rebuild: <code>python docs/reports/modules/tug/build_report.py</code>. The calculation data are embedded in this HTML. Styles are copied from <code>docs/api/cfd/turbulent-flat-plate-verification.html</code> and <code>docs/api/_assets/brand.css</code>.</li></ul>
